    "Indonesian immigration officials prevented 39 citizens from traveling to Russia over suspicions they were trafficking victims recruited as soldiers.",
    "The intervention follows reports of an Indonesian man from Kebumen who allegedly died after being recruited as a mercenary for the Russian military.",
    "The Indonesian House of Representatives has called for a comprehensive mapping of citizens abroad as government agencies continue efforts to intercept recruits."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "Indonesian authorities have intensified efforts to stop citizens from joining the Russian military as mercenaries. Recent operations by the Directorate General of Immigration and police have successfully intercepted dozens of individuals attempting to depart the country. These actions follow emerging reports of fatalities, including a man from Kebumen, who reportedly died after traveling to participate in the conflict. Government officials and members of the House of Representatives have expressed concern over human trafficking networks allegedly facilitating these recruitments. The Ministry of Foreign Affairs is exploring options to repatriate citizens who may have been coerced or deceived into service. This series of events has prompted legislative calls for better oversight and documentation of Indonesian nationals currently abroad, amid fears that others may be vulnerable to recruitment schemes promising economic opportunities but leading to military involvement.",
